Backport the fixes relevant to the julia 1.13.1 RISC-V test failures from:
https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/commit/40fc452472de3a507416a081735e10f5fbf2be07
https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/commit/7a4d8bc946262a86366815b6090039b36620c03d
https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/commit/a8e80a77933dd3393b65916c5a5c6c5d54195539
https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/commit/3d592bf9ebaa42ad2426db07ebe5cfa5332602fb
https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/commit/feeb3be2749ccb88c0368a4651933cd63f3aa2d7

Also allow the slower RISC-V builders 200x the nominal compile-time sanity
threshold; the logged 6.74-second value only exceeded the generic limit by 12%.

Use libuv's existing fork and close-on-exec error-pipe path on RISC-V because
the bundled version's vfork path lost the shared exec-error value and made a
missing executable exit 127 instead of making uv_spawn report ENOENT. Upstream
later replaced this path as part of:
https://github.com/JuliaLang/libuv/commit/40d45efebf9bf1a8091a573d26e53d9c4262ef5b

Extend the RISC-V thread watchdog to one hour because the logged run was still
executing peakflops tests when the generic 20-minute watchdog fired:
https://archriscv.felixc.at/.status/logs/julia/julia-2%3A1.13.0-2.log

Allow ten times longer for RISC-V prompt challenges and interrupt-test output.
The September 25 run killed secretbuffer's child during LLVM compilation and
sent SIGINT before the REPL had finished compiling its error-display path.
Keep the upstream synchronization and assertions from:
https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/commit/d4f184f3640c9643e5b637f70b86461fef3fc5e7

Use the existing rr worker-removal allowance on RISC-V too. The failed misc
worker was still compiling _atexit when the 30-second removal deadline aborted
the suite, before Distributed's 15 + 6 + 15-second kill sequence could finish:
https://github.com/JuliaLang/Distributed.jl/blob/661112ef29b8d371b8612b94a629c0bbcf3d36f7/src/managers.jl

Extend the remaining SIGINT process-exit wait on RISC-V: the September 27 run
still found the child running after three 10-second waits. Keep checking that
it exits with InterruptException rather than skipping the signal test.

Also accept minute-prefixed durations in the custom TestCounts summary. This
covers the same 1m04.8s output rejected by the other summary tests, beyond:
https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/commit/4ef42fe7273fbbf025bc9b196f55f7df86b516a0

Backport per-expression compilation of the thread tests and smaller task-metrics
workloads to reduce watchdog pressure, preserving all tests and the longer
RISC-V safety deadline. The upstream patch needs adaptation to 1.13.0's file
boundaries:
https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/commit/0d695bd737a817cbb40c676b896faee9bf929db6

Restore the upstream vector assertions: the native 1.13.1 build reports all
36 locally marked cases as unexpected passes, with no other test errors:
https://archriscv.felixc.at/.status/logs/julia/julia-2%3A1.13.1-1.log

